From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Armada <armada@armada-os.org>
Date: Thu, 18 Sep 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] backlight: sy7758: make the enable GPIO optional

The AYANEO Pocket DS wires no discrete enable line to its SY7758, and the
accepted driver requires one, which left the whole lower DSI chain in
probe deferral. Make the GPIO optional in the driver and drop it from the
binding's required list; boards that do describe one are unaffected.

Armada-only delta on top of the accepted upstream driver and binding.
---
diff --git a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/leds/backlight/silergy,sy7758.yaml b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/leds/backlight/silergy,sy7758.yaml
index 64af6b346..bf1d9c2b8 100644
--- a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/leds/backlight/silergy,sy7758.yaml
+++ b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/leds/backlight/silergy,sy7758.yaml
@@ -31,7 +31,6 @@ properties:
 required:
   - compatible
   - reg
-  - enable-gpios
 
 unevaluatedProperties: false
 
diff --git a/drivers/video/backlight/sy7758.c b/drivers/video/backlight/sy7758.c
index 786589cb8..a36019a92 100644
--- a/drivers/video/backlight/sy7758.c
+++ b/drivers/video/backlight/sy7758.c
@@ -184,8 +184,11 @@ static int sy7758_probe(struct i2c_client *client)
 
 	fsleep(100);
 
-	/* Get enable GPIO and set to high */
-	sydev->gpio = devm_gpiod_get(dev, "enable", GPIOD_OUT_HIGH);
+	/*
+	 * Some boards route SY7758 EN through a dedicated GPIO, while Pocket DS
+	 * leaves the chip reachable without a separately-described enable pin.
+	 */
+	sydev->gpio = devm_gpiod_get_optional(dev, "enable", GPIOD_OUT_HIGH);
 	if (IS_ERR(sydev->gpio))
 		return dev_err_probe(dev, PTR_ERR(sydev->gpio),
 				     "failed to get enable GPIO\n");
